<title>UK: Yorkshire Electricity chairman resigns.</title>
<headline>Yorkshire Electricity chairman resigns.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yorkshire Electricity Group Plc said on Thursday that non-executive director and chairman Christopher Hampson, and non-executive directors Lady Eccles of Moulton, John Robins, Sir Philip Beck and John Hardman had announced their resignations from the board with effect from 5 April 1997.</p>
<p>The resignations follow the agreed takeover of Yorkshire, one of Britain's last remaining independent electricity companies, by American Electric power Co Inc and Public Service Co of Colorado for 1.5 billion pounds ($2.5 billion).</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
